To retrieve a Payment by ID, use the GET operation on the Payment resource with the specific payment ID in the path.

**Endpoint:**
GET /payment/{id}

**Description:**
This operation retrieves a payment entity. Attribute selection is enabled for all first-level attributes. Filtering on sub-resources may be available depending on the compliance level supported by an implementation [TMF676 | Page 35 | Chunk TMF676_0043].

**Request Example:**
GET serverRoot/paymentManagement/v4/payment/12345 Accept: application/json

**Response Example (200 OK):**
{
  "id": "12345",
  "href": "https://host:port/paymentManagement/v4/payment/12345",
  "correlatorId": "67890",
  "paymentDate": "2020-01-08T12:06:38.230Z",
  "name": "Example",
  "description": "a payment example",
  "status": "done",
  "statusDate": "2020-01-08T12:06:38.230Z",
  "@type": "Payment",
  "amount": {
    "unit": "EUR",
    "value": 10
  },
  "taxAmount": {
    "unit": "EUR",
    "value": 1.6
  },
  "totalAmount": {
    "unit": "EUR",
    "value": 11.6
  },
  "channel": {
    ...
  }
} [TMF676 | Page 35 | Chunk TMF676_0043]

To update a customer's contact information, use the PATCH method on the customer resource endpoint with a JSON Patch request.

The `contactMedium` attribute is patchable [TMF629_0047]. For example, to update the preferred status of a contact medium in Paris, use the following request:

PATCH /customer/{id}  
Content-Type: application/json-patch-query+json  
[  
  {  
    "op": "replace",  
    "path": "/contactMedium/preferred?city=Paris",  
    "value": true  
  }  
]  

This example modifies the `preferred` field of a `GeographicAddressContactMedium` where the `city` is "Paris" [TMF629_0055]. The `contactMedium` sub-resource includes fields such as `preferred`, `contactType`, `validFor`, and `city`, which are part of the customer's contact information [TMF629_0054]. The `@type` field of the contact medium (e.g., `PhoneContactMedium` or `GeographicAddressContactMedium`) identifies the type of contact medium [TMF629_0024].
